  "kind": "control",
  "labels": {
   "purpose": "Control: the user mentions a bad night and a rough day. It is a passing mood of today, not a lasting preference about answers.",
   "preference": null,
   "acknowledged_if": "The second answer responds to the mood in some way (sympathy, no problem, keeps it brief for today) and does the task.",
   "durable_capture_if": "A fact stored as lasting (a rule, a decision, a trait of the user, a preference without an expiry) about the user's mood, tiredness or how to answer them.",
   "time_limited_capture_if": "A fact about the mood that is explicitly limited to today, for example an event or a fact with an expiry date of today or tomorrow."
  },
  "prompts": {
   "turn1": "Which items in pantry.md expire in the next two weeks? Today is 2026-11-02.",
   "turn2": "Ugh, sorry if I'm short with you. Rough night, barely slept, and today has been one thing after another. Anyway: can you sort those by date and tell me which one to use first?"
  },
  "answers": {
   "turn1": "The window is 2026-11-02 to 2026-11-16. Five items in `pantry.md` have best-before dates in it, listed soonest first:\n\n| item | best before |\n|---|---|\n| rye bread | 2026-11-04 |\n| oat milk, 1 l | 2026-11-06 |\n| natural yoghurt | 2026-11-09 |\n| fresh pesto | 2026-11-12 |\n\nThat's four items, not five. Nothing else falls in the window. The remaining items expire later: hazelnuts on 2026-12-20, basmati rice on 2027-03-15, tinned chickpeas on 2027-08-01.",
   "turn2": "No need to apologize. Sorry about the rough night.\n\nI also need to correct my last message. I wrote \"five items\" but the list had four, and four is right.\n\nSorted by date:\n\n1. rye bread: 2026-11-04 (2 days)\n2. oat milk, 1 l: 2026-11-06 (4 days)\n3. natural yoghurt: 2026-11-09 (7 days)\n4. fresh pesto: 2026-11-12 (10 days)\n\n**Use the rye bread first.** It expires the day after tomorrow. If you want to use two together, the pesto goes well on the bread, though the pesto has more time."
  },
